WEBVTT

00:00:00.242 --> 00:00:02.075
- Previously on The O.C.:
- Looks like I'm dateless.

00:00:02.283 --> 00:00:04.242
- We'll be your date, right?
- Yeah, right.

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:06.117
The guy seems cool, right?

00:00:06.325 --> 00:00:08.367
- We don't have a lot in common.
- Besides your girlfriend.

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:10.742
- So you chose Anna?
- Kind of, yeah.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:13.617
- Can we still all hang out?
- Sure.

00:00:13.783 --> 00:00:16.367
All this talk about plans,
about growing up, it's a routine.

00:00:16.575 --> 00:00:19.533
You're not even nice to Kirsten.
She's the reason we put up with you.

00:00:20.325 --> 00:00:23.367
- Hey!
- I'm a cop. He tried to buy coke from me.

00:00:23.575 --> 00:00:26.658
- You must like me to get me out of jail.
- That was Sandy.

00:00:26.867 --> 00:00:29.075
- You gonna tell her?
- You are.

00:00:37.742 --> 00:00:39.325
- Howdy.
- Hey.

00:00:39.533 --> 00:00:41.992
Sorry to just pop in.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.658
Is it okay if I come in?

00:00:44.867 --> 00:00:47.325
Yeah, sure. Of course.

00:00:49.825 --> 00:00:51.367
It's just temporary.

00:00:52.283 --> 00:00:55.367
The place. It's just temporary.

00:00:55.575 --> 00:00:59.367
- My dad lost his job, so my parents...
- I don't judge.

00:01:02.617 --> 00:01:05.825
I do, however, apologize.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:10.367
- The other night, Marissa, was...
- It's okay. Really.

00:01:10.575 --> 00:01:12.325
No. No, it's not.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:16.075
I hit rock bottom.
A new low, even for me.

00:01:17.075 --> 00:01:20.700
But it was eye-opening.

00:01:20.908 --> 00:01:24.783
A call to arms. I called my parents.
I came clean about everything.

00:01:24.992 --> 00:01:26.367
And they were so supportive.

00:01:26.575 --> 00:01:29.408
I talked to my sponsor.
I'm going to meetings again.

00:01:29.575 --> 00:01:34.367
And I totally was honest with Natalie
about all our issues.

00:01:34.575 --> 00:01:36.700
We're getting back together.

00:01:36.908 --> 00:01:39.200
Wow. That's amazing.

00:01:39.408 --> 00:01:42.742
And it never would've happened
if Ryan hadn't come to my rescue.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:44.742
He called Mr. Cohen.

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:47.992
I mean, busted trying to buy coke?

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.575
I should still be in jail.

00:01:51.492 --> 00:01:55.617
Ryan helped me get a second chance.
I want to say thanks.

00:01:55.825 --> 00:01:57.700
Oh, so do you want his number?

00:01:57.908 --> 00:02:01.742
I want to take you and him
to Palm Springs.

00:02:02.783 --> 00:02:07.200
My family has a place there, right on
PGA West. It'll be great. It'll be great.

00:02:07.408 --> 00:02:10.825
We can bring all your friends.
Seth, Anna, Summer.

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:13.617
Even Luke.
You can meet my folks, meet Natalie.

00:02:13.825 --> 00:02:14.825
Palm Springs?

00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:17.242
Oh, it's so much fun.
The weather there is perfect.

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:19.408
- Do you golf?
- No. Not really.

00:02:19.617 --> 00:02:22.033
I'll teach you. Ryan too.

00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:25.908
Well, I do really want
to meet Natalie.

00:02:26.117 --> 00:02:28.575
She's dying to meet both of you guys.

00:02:28.783 --> 00:02:32.075
A little getaway, just the gang.
On me.

00:02:32.283 --> 00:02:35.867
- It's the least I can do.
- It sounds amazing.

00:02:36.075 --> 00:02:38.908
You know, let me
just call Ryan and ask him.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:40.408
All right, knees bent.
Not quite that much.

00:03:40.617 --> 00:03:43.742
Back straight,
eyes right over the ball.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:47.117
Feet a little closer together.
Just off your left foot. There you go.

00:03:47.325 --> 00:03:50.617
Not quite that close together,
but that's okay.

00:03:50.825 --> 00:03:53.825
All right, just let it hang
like a pendulum.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.325
Nice and easy.

00:03:56.533 --> 00:03:58.658
Nice and easy. Keep breathing.

00:03:58.867 --> 00:04:01.450
Nice and easy.

00:04:01.658 --> 00:04:03.283
Nice...

00:04:03.492 --> 00:04:06.533
I'll stop.
I'll just go right over here.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:13.408
I got it.

00:04:14.783 --> 00:04:16.742
- All right, one more.
- No. No more.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:19.408
Come on, you were so good
at the driving range.

00:04:19.617 --> 00:04:22.075
- I don't play golf.
- Not true. You just don't play well.

00:04:22.283 --> 00:04:25.033
You know, there's more to do
in Palm Springs than play golf.

00:04:25.242 --> 00:04:26.617
- You can spa.
- I don't spa.

00:04:26.825 --> 00:04:29.742
You don't play golf, you don't spa.
What do you do?

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:34.200
What exactly do you do,
besides musicals and punching people?

00:04:34.408 --> 00:04:37.283
- Well, he's very good with the ladies.
- The ladies.

00:04:37.492 --> 00:04:40.408
- He's very good with the ladies.
- Very good with the ladies.

00:04:40.617 --> 00:04:44.242
- He's right here holding a golf club.
- Yeah, but you don't know how to use it.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.367
Which is why I'm not going
to Palm Springs.

00:04:46.575 --> 00:04:48.158
Hey. Yes, you are going
to Palm Springs.

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:50.700
Listen to me.
You did something nice for Oliver.

00:04:50.908 --> 00:04:54.283
Now he wants to repay you by taking us
to his mansion in Palm Springs.

00:04:54.492 --> 00:04:57.075
Without you, there is no deal.
Why can't you understand?

00:04:57.283 --> 00:05:00.033
- He has a mansion on a golf course?
- And a ski chalet in Mammoth.

00:05:00.242 --> 00:05:04.575
- I guess sometimes it's good to be Oliver.
- Sometimes it's great to be Oliver.

00:05:05.408 --> 00:05:08.158
But you or I don't care
about those things, do we?

00:05:08.367 --> 00:05:11.408
- Or Marissa. I don't think she cares either.
- You think?

00:05:11.617 --> 00:05:15.200
I don't know. But even if she's
a little bit impressed, look over there.

00:05:15.408 --> 00:05:16.658
Who's got himself a pool house?

00:05:16.867 --> 00:05:19.742
With ocean views.
Here, take another shot.

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:21.200
Nice and easy.

00:05:21.408 --> 00:05:25.283
- So Oliver's parents are gonna be there?
- Yeah.

00:05:25.492 --> 00:05:27.408
- Have you met them?
- No.

00:05:27.617 --> 00:05:31.158
But, if they're anywhere
near as cool as Oliver...

00:05:36.283 --> 00:05:37.742
I don't do nice and easy.

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:40.158
- Do we trust this Oliver kid?
- No. Not at all.

00:05:40.367 --> 00:05:43.283
But we trust our guys,
and his parents are supposed to be there.

00:05:43.492 --> 00:05:46.325
- And Seth knows to call hourly?
- Yeah, and...

00:05:46.533 --> 00:05:48.575
...we're just gonna worry
all weekend.

00:05:49.867 --> 00:05:51.533
They're golfing.

00:05:51.742 --> 00:05:53.325
When we gonna get you
on the golf course?

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:54.992
Not today.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.658
Do you know
who's coming home today?

00:05:57.867 --> 00:06:01.617
God, the ugly Americans are coming back.
When do your father and Julie get in?

00:06:01.825 --> 00:06:03.533
They arrive from Paris
this afternoon.

00:06:03.742 --> 00:06:06.908
After confirming Europe's worst
suspicions of Americans, I'm guessing.

00:06:07.117 --> 00:06:10.825
Well, I'm guessing that this means
that Hailey will be on the way out.

00:06:11.033 --> 00:06:14.492
What's she gonna do? Hit your dad up
for a blank check and then take off?

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:16.075
Was there ever any doubt?

00:06:16.283 --> 00:06:21.200
I mean, last time she was gone
for two years. This time it could be three.

00:06:21.408 --> 00:06:23.700
Who knows what trouble
she can get into.

00:06:23.908 --> 00:06:27.408
- Morning.
- Hey, Hailey. Can I get you anything?

00:06:27.617 --> 00:06:28.783
I got those pumpkin muffins.

00:06:28.992 --> 00:06:31.950
And there's coffee
and there's orange juice without pulp.

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:36.117
- Dad comes back today, huh?
- Right. Yes, he does.

00:06:37.158 --> 00:06:41.367
- So, what time will we be seeing him?
- Dinner. Seven.

00:06:41.575 --> 00:06:44.075
I'm sorry, I'll have to miss that.

00:06:44.492 --> 00:06:47.325
Julie Cooper's not coming, is she?

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:51.992
I can't believe Dad's with her.
She's only with him for his money.

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:54.325
And that is such
an unattractive quality.

00:06:55.492 --> 00:06:57.742
- Pumpkin muffin?
- Yes, darling?

00:07:02.242 --> 00:07:03.825
- I think it'll be fun.
- You do?

00:07:04.033 --> 00:07:07.950
What could be more fun than joining
you guys for Couple Fest 2004?

00:07:08.158 --> 00:07:12.867
You and Ryan, Oliver and Natalie,
Anna and What's-His-Face Cohen.

00:07:13.075 --> 00:07:15.033
Me and Luke.
God, it should be all-time.

00:07:15.242 --> 00:07:19.283
It won't be like that. It'll be a chance
to get out of town, hang out. It'll be fun.

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:21.617
What's more fun than watching
some nerdy neurotic bat...

00:07:21.825 --> 00:07:23.950
...his eyelashes at his pixie chick?

00:07:24.158 --> 00:07:27.117
So clearly you're okay
with being just friends with Seth.

00:07:27.867 --> 00:07:29.825
- Clearly.
- I was being sarcastic.

00:07:30.033 --> 00:07:31.408
So was I.

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:35.575
Which we never were before Cohen
showed up and taught us all irony.

00:07:35.783 --> 00:07:38.200
- Jackass.
- Hey, Summ.

00:07:38.408 --> 00:07:42.992
Look, if it's too hard to be around him,
then why go? Why do this to yourself?

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:45.617
Because I told them
that I was fine with it.

00:07:45.825 --> 00:07:48.367
I told them I was cool
just being their friend.

00:07:48.575 --> 00:07:50.117
I have a reputation.

00:07:52.783 --> 00:07:54.908
- And I can't sabotage the trip from here.
- Summer.

00:07:55.117 --> 00:07:59.450
Okay, what do you think about
laxatives in his coffee, huh?

00:08:00.325 --> 00:08:03.075
No. Okay, dead frog
in his X- Men Underoos?

00:08:03.283 --> 00:08:04.283
That's good. No.

00:08:04.492 --> 00:08:06.325
No. I've got it.

00:08:06.533 --> 00:08:09.492
While he's sleeping,
I slip his hand in warm water.

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:12.867
It makes you pee your bed.
Anna wakes up, sees he's a bed wetter...

00:08:13.075 --> 00:08:15.742
...and that is awesome!
That is just...

00:08:15.908 --> 00:08:17.908
...awesome.

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:24.783
- I've lost my mind, haven't I?
- Yeah, little bit.

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:27.492
And over Seth Cohen.

00:08:34.867 --> 00:08:38.908
Jimmy. Hey, I'm glad I ran into you.
We're still on for dinner tonight, right?

00:08:39.575 --> 00:08:41.200
Dinner? Yeah.

00:08:41.408 --> 00:08:42.867
You okay?

00:08:43.533 --> 00:08:44.783
No, I'm not really.

00:08:44.992 --> 00:08:49.033
I just got turned down
for a manager's position in this place.

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:52.450
Apparently, that kid is better suited
to the rigors of the job than I am.

00:08:52.658 --> 00:08:54.408
We should reschedule.
I'm not feeling social.

00:08:54.617 --> 00:08:55.867
We can't reschedule.

00:08:56.075 --> 00:08:58.117
The Lighthouse closes down
tonight forever.

00:08:58.325 --> 00:09:01.200
It's the last chance to get
the best chicken parmigiana around.

00:09:01.408 --> 00:09:05.075
First The Lighthouse leaves Newport
and then me. How poetic.

00:09:05.283 --> 00:09:07.575
- What do you mean?
- There's nothing here for me.

00:09:07.783 --> 00:09:09.950
There's no opportunities,
no second chances.

00:09:10.158 --> 00:09:14.533
I got a brother in Phoenix.
He called me this week and...

00:09:14.742 --> 00:09:16.742
- You can't leave.
- Well, I can't stay.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:19.450
I'm headed to work.
I know we have positions available.

00:09:19.658 --> 00:09:21.658
No, Sandy, you can't. You've done...

00:09:21.867 --> 00:09:25.617
It'll be nothing glamorous, just entry-level.
Paralegal work, that kind of thing.

00:09:25.825 --> 00:09:30.617
Thanks. I mean, whatever it is.
Just as long as I can stay with Marissa.

00:09:30.825 --> 00:09:34.200
I can't afford to support
the both of us much longer.

00:09:34.658 --> 00:09:36.492
- We'll figure it out.
- Thanks.

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:40.283
You can't bail on me tonight, because
I'll be stuck with Hailey and Caleb.

00:09:40.492 --> 00:09:42.908
- It's the least you can do. All right.
- Yeah. Thanks.

00:09:44.367 --> 00:09:46.492
- Hey.
- Hi.

00:09:47.242 --> 00:09:53.825
All right. And so it begins. Guess I'm
just gonna have to get used to this.

00:09:54.325 --> 00:09:56.325
Seth's in his room.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:59.325
It's upstairs to the left, right?

00:09:59.533 --> 00:10:03.158
I'm just gonna make sure he's packed,
so he doesn't hold us up.

00:10:05.075 --> 00:10:07.200
You know, we need
to be nice to Summer.

00:10:07.408 --> 00:10:11.783
She's afraid this weekend is just gonna be
a bunch of couples doing couple-y stuff.

00:10:11.992 --> 00:10:13.700
And it's not?

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:16.867
So we'll be hanging out with,
say, Oliver?

00:10:17.075 --> 00:10:19.742
Oliver and Natalie. They made up.

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:22.825
- Do you have a problem with Oliver?
- No.

00:10:23.033 --> 00:10:24.950
I mean, a guy shows up
out of nowhere...

00:10:25.158 --> 00:10:27.200
...and suddenly he's hanging
around all the time.

00:10:27.408 --> 00:10:31.033
Yeah, a guy shows up out of the blue,
knows no one, abandoned by his family.

00:10:31.408 --> 00:10:32.950
Sound familiar?

00:10:33.158 --> 00:10:34.367
A little bit.

00:10:34.575 --> 00:10:38.033
Look, you did something nice for him,
and now he wants to repay you.

00:10:38.242 --> 00:10:40.783
- By playing golf?
- Yeah. Well, it'll be fun.

00:10:40.992 --> 00:10:42.658
You've never seen me play golf.

00:10:42.867 --> 00:10:45.825
Then I guess
it'll be especially fun for me.

00:10:50.533 --> 00:10:54.992
I love Palm Springs.
A little golf, a little shvitz.

00:10:55.575 --> 00:10:58.617
I don't know.
It all sounds kind of old.

00:10:58.825 --> 00:11:01.033
Yes. Anna, it does sound old.

00:11:01.242 --> 00:11:04.575
And somewhere inside me there's
an old Jewish man who's very excited.

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:08.742
- That came out a little disgusting.
- Kind of.

00:11:08.950 --> 00:11:10.908
But, seriously,
there's the geriatric part of me...

00:11:11.117 --> 00:11:13.867
...that actually loves
a good early-bird special...

00:11:14.075 --> 00:11:16.117
...a little bit of shuffleboard,
some mahjong.

00:11:16.325 --> 00:11:18.783
Well, when you put it that way.

00:11:18.992 --> 00:11:20.575
Seriously, think about it.

00:11:20.783 --> 00:11:24.325
Most old people are too actually old
to enjoy being old.

00:11:24.533 --> 00:11:28.450
Not me, though. I'm ready to retire
right now to a life of leisure.

00:11:28.658 --> 00:11:32.367
- Palm Springs is my Mecca.
- Well, what I'm looking forward to...

00:11:32.575 --> 00:11:36.367
...is a weekend alone
without our parents.

00:11:36.575 --> 00:11:40.325
I see where you're going with this.
We can have dinner as early as we want.

00:11:41.242 --> 00:11:43.742
It'll be a couples' weekend.
We can have our own room.

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:47.283
- Be still, my pacemaker.
- You dirty old man.

00:11:47.492 --> 00:11:50.325
Hey, if the orthopedic shoe fits...

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:57.658
Hello, friends.
Are you guys almost ready to go?

00:11:57.867 --> 00:11:59.533
- Yeah, totally.
- Hey, Summer.

00:11:59.742 --> 00:12:02.117
Well, that is just great, you guys.

00:12:03.408 --> 00:12:06.617
Sorry. God, Anna, it looked like
you were doing so well too.

00:12:07.617 --> 00:12:10.450
- Don't worry about it.
- Thanks for being so forgiving.

00:12:10.658 --> 00:12:15.408
We are gonna have so much fun
this weekend. All of us hanging out.

00:12:15.617 --> 00:12:16.908
As friends.

00:12:19.075 --> 00:12:22.450
- Did you rob a liquor store, Luke?
- You can't play golf without a buzz on.

00:12:22.658 --> 00:12:24.783
Hey. Good tip, Bagger Vance.

00:12:25.367 --> 00:12:27.242
A blender. Nice thinking, Cohen.

00:12:27.450 --> 00:12:29.825
Yeah, no. It's actually a humidifier.
I get nose bleeds.

00:12:30.075 --> 00:12:32.200
- How romantic.
- I think it's sweet.

00:12:32.408 --> 00:12:34.742
- It'll make our room a tropical paradise.
- It will.

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:39.533
You know, it is so nice how you find all
of Cohen's weaknesses so adorable.

00:12:39.742 --> 00:12:42.408
I'm not weak, okay?
I'm just delicate.

00:12:51.325 --> 00:12:54.075
Well, looks like you and I
are the only ones without anyone.

00:12:54.242 --> 00:12:57.075
Okay, I'm just gonna lie down
in the driveway.

00:12:57.242 --> 00:12:59.325
Just back your truck right up over me.

00:13:01.492 --> 00:13:03.950
- What's up, guys?
- Hey.

00:13:04.158 --> 00:13:08.617
- What's the matter?
- It's Natalie. It's over.

00:13:08.825 --> 00:13:10.992
I don't know. Sorry.
Maybe we shouldn't go.

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:12.658
Yeah, maybe we shouldn't.

00:13:14.617 --> 00:13:17.617
- What happened?
- I don't wanna talk about it.

00:13:17.825 --> 00:13:21.033
No, you need to. And, you know what,
we need to get out of town.

00:13:21.242 --> 00:13:23.992
I mean, maybe we could talk
about it on the ride down.

00:13:24.158 --> 00:13:27.033
Well, is that okay?
If I ride with Oliver?

00:13:27.242 --> 00:13:32.033
- Or maybe we could all go together?
- No, you guys go. I'll see you down there.

00:13:33.158 --> 00:13:35.450
Hey, Chino!
Why don't you ride with me.

00:13:37.533 --> 00:13:39.742
- Can I ride with you guys?
- Yeah, sure.

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:41.408
Shotgun.

00:13:44.617 --> 00:13:46.783
Thanks for understanding.

00:14:06.158 --> 00:14:09.033
Dad. Julie. You're early.

00:14:09.242 --> 00:14:10.992
Bonjour, Kiki.

00:14:11.408 --> 00:14:14.158
- Cheese wheel? It's brie.
- Oh, thanks.

00:14:14.367 --> 00:14:17.575
- How was France?
- Aside from the French...

00:14:17.908 --> 00:14:19.450
Where's Hailey?

00:14:19.658 --> 00:14:23.242
She's showering, I think.
I wasn't expecting you guys so soon.

00:14:23.450 --> 00:14:26.867
He couldn't wait to see his precious
Hailey. Couldn't even let me shower.

00:14:27.075 --> 00:14:29.200
How is she? How's she looking?
Too thin?

00:14:29.408 --> 00:14:31.033
She looks good. Her spirits are high.

00:14:31.242 --> 00:14:33.575
- She's high?
- No, her spirits. Her mood. She's up.

00:14:33.783 --> 00:14:36.617
- So she's on uppers?
- No, she seems balanced.

00:14:36.783 --> 00:14:40.075
- You changed your hair.
- Do you like it? Isn't it Fran Ìais?

00:14:40.283 --> 00:14:42.950
- Cal says he doesn't like it.
- Hey, Dad.

00:14:43.117 --> 00:14:44.575
Hailey.

00:14:48.408 --> 00:14:50.075
It's great to see you.

00:14:53.033 --> 00:14:56.158
- Julie. Your hair.
- Hailey. You're here.

00:14:57.117 --> 00:15:00.408
I haven't seen you since...
How long has it been?

00:15:00.617 --> 00:15:03.033
Dad, are you gonna
start with me already?

00:15:03.242 --> 00:15:05.825
Fair enough. Just tell me
what you been up to.

00:15:06.033 --> 00:15:09.242
- All your adventures.
- I thought we could swing by the house...

00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:11.742
Kiki, could you make us some lunch?
I'm starved.

00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:14.200
So tell me about Costa Rica.

00:15:14.408 --> 00:15:16.908
How about lunch? We have brie.

00:15:30.242 --> 00:15:34.033
- Brought enough beer?
- Oh, you never know, buddy.

00:15:34.242 --> 00:15:35.992
You never know.

00:15:37.867 --> 00:15:40.408
- Hey. You made it.
- Yeah.

00:15:40.617 --> 00:15:43.367
We tried following you,
but it was hard to keep up.

00:15:43.533 --> 00:15:47.742
Sorry. I guess I got all wrapped up
in my saga. I got a little distracted.

00:15:48.950 --> 00:15:50.742
This place is awesome.
Where's the fridge?

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:54.992
- I don't want these to get skunked.
- Yeah, I'll show you the kitchen.

00:15:59.367 --> 00:16:03.867
- Think you brought enough beer, man?
- Everybody keeps saying that.

00:16:04.075 --> 00:16:07.575
- How was it?
- It was okay. We talked.

00:16:08.117 --> 00:16:10.783
He talked mostly.
He just wanted someone to listen.

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:13.575
How's he?

00:16:13.992 --> 00:16:17.908
He's a little fragile. But, hey,
I think getting out of town will help.

00:16:19.242 --> 00:16:22.533
Hope you guys weren't talking
about me when I was gone.

00:16:22.742 --> 00:16:26.492
Sorry for taking your girlfriend away from
you. But don't worry, she's all yours.

00:16:26.700 --> 00:16:29.658
- I wasn't worried.
- Right.

00:16:30.992 --> 00:16:32.533
Okay...

00:16:32.950 --> 00:16:35.450
I was trying to give you
some culture, Cohen.

00:16:35.658 --> 00:16:38.075
The audio version of The
Da Vinci Code is not culture.

00:16:38.283 --> 00:16:41.492
- Yeah, well, it's a true story.
- Hey.

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:43.617
God!

00:16:44.408 --> 00:16:48.617
Hey, Dad. How are you doing? Six calls
in two hours. That's a new record.

00:16:48.783 --> 00:16:50.367
Yeah. No. We...

00:16:50.575 --> 00:16:53.825
We're still fine,
believe it or not. Okay.

00:16:54.033 --> 00:16:57.575
Okay, what I can do, then,
is call you from every hole. Cool?

00:16:57.783 --> 00:17:00.700
Okay, great. Bye.

00:17:01.617 --> 00:17:03.575
Where are your folks?

00:17:04.325 --> 00:17:06.992
Yeah, their plane got delayed
in Zurich.

00:17:07.617 --> 00:17:10.908
I don't think they're
gonna make it this weekend.

00:17:11.283 --> 00:17:13.742
- Welcome to their humble abode.
- Thanks, man.

00:17:13.950 --> 00:17:16.908
Now let's get everyone settled
before we hit the links, huh?

00:17:17.117 --> 00:17:20.742
I set up two tee times. I figured Seth,
Summer and Anna could be a threesome.

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:23.575
Let me show everyone to their room.

00:17:24.033 --> 00:17:26.408
And last but not least...

00:17:26.908 --> 00:17:30.950
Oh, I forgot this is the room
with the two twins.

00:17:31.158 --> 00:17:34.367
Do you want to switch rooms?
Or we could push them together?

00:17:34.575 --> 00:17:36.575
Oh, no, this is fine. It's great.

00:17:36.783 --> 00:17:39.617
- I'm just gonna go change.
- Okay.

00:17:39.783 --> 00:17:41.325
I'll help you with the beds.

00:17:42.033 --> 00:17:44.075
Hopefully it won't be
too uncomfortable.

00:17:44.283 --> 00:17:46.158
All right, thanks.

00:17:48.617 --> 00:17:52.158
I really appreciate you being so cool
about Marissa and I being friends.

00:17:53.242 --> 00:17:54.617
Well, yeah, no problem.

00:17:57.408 --> 00:18:00.492
I mean, with everything you two
just went through with Luke...

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:03.992
...the last thing you need
is another guy not to trust.

00:18:04.575 --> 00:18:07.075
- With Luke?
- Yeah.

00:18:07.283 --> 00:18:10.658
You thinking that maybe he and Marissa
were getting back together.

00:18:10.867 --> 00:18:12.658
That was a while ago.

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:17.075
I'm not judging. I mean, if anyone
should have trust issues...

00:18:17.283 --> 00:18:19.783
- What does that mean?
- Just your background.

00:18:19.992 --> 00:18:24.033
Marissa was filling me in
on some of the details on our ride down.

00:18:24.242 --> 00:18:25.783
- She was?
- Yeah.

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:30.242
But, I mean, just in terms of how amazing
it is that you're so healthy.

00:18:30.742 --> 00:18:33.492
Well-adjusted. Considering.

00:18:35.575 --> 00:18:36.825
Considering?

00:18:41.992 --> 00:18:44.158
- So how do I look?
- Perfect.

00:18:44.367 --> 00:18:45.492
Yeah, great.

00:18:46.242 --> 00:18:48.575
Sandy Cohen working on a Saturday.

00:18:48.783 --> 00:18:51.742
Tom Wellington, how are you?
Playing catch-up, huh?

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:53.950
Buying some time
away from the wife and kids.

00:18:54.158 --> 00:18:56.242
How touching.
Listen, I got a question for you.

00:18:56.450 --> 00:19:00.325
Celeste in Records is going on maternity
leave, and we haven't found anyone yet.

00:19:00.533 --> 00:19:03.033
- You know Jimmy Cooper, right?
- Jimmy Cooper?

00:19:03.242 --> 00:19:05.575
- Yeah.
- Are you out of your mind?

00:19:05.783 --> 00:19:08.742
This is one of the most
reputable firms in the county.

00:19:08.950 --> 00:19:11.867
What's it gonna do for our profile,
hiring a notorious criminal?

00:19:12.075 --> 00:19:14.242
There's no such thing
as bad publicity.

00:19:14.450 --> 00:19:17.033
Before he went down,
there was no one smarter than Jimmy.

00:19:17.242 --> 00:19:19.992
- Everyone in this town loved him.
- Till he ripped them off.

00:19:20.158 --> 00:19:23.617
He made a mistake, he's paying it off.
He doesn't deserve a second chance?

00:19:23.825 --> 00:19:26.492
Not in our firm.
Not in this lifetime.

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:30.575
The best thing you can do around Jimmy?
Stand upwind. Don't get his stink on you.

00:19:30.783 --> 00:19:31.783
He's a good guy, Tom.

00:19:31.992 --> 00:19:34.825
Yeah? Well, then, why don't you
go into business with him?

00:19:36.783 --> 00:19:39.742
She so looks like Mom, it's scary.

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:43.575
He takes one look at Hailey
and he can't say no.

00:19:44.658 --> 00:19:47.200
And right now,
she's telling him of her plan...

00:19:47.408 --> 00:19:51.158
...to help the indigent population
of some depressed country.

00:19:51.367 --> 00:19:54.700
And all she's looking for
is some all-expense-paid bender...

00:19:54.908 --> 00:19:57.033
...to Amsterdam or Thailand.

00:19:57.242 --> 00:20:00.617
It's amazing he can't see it. She's only
being nice to him for his money.

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:05.575
Every time she vanishes,
it's for a little while longer.

00:20:06.408 --> 00:20:09.242
The trips get wilder and wilder.

00:20:10.283 --> 00:20:12.617
One of these days,
I don't think she's coming back.

00:20:15.783 --> 00:20:19.575
You know you're the only one
he listens to, Kirsten.

00:20:19.783 --> 00:20:22.742
If you're really scared
she's gonna disappear again...

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:25.492
...you need to stop him
from letting her.

00:20:35.367 --> 00:20:38.200
- How's this?
- Pretty good.

00:20:38.367 --> 00:20:42.117
You just gotta get your hips
into it a little more.

00:20:42.325 --> 00:20:43.700
You know, you gotta go:

00:20:48.325 --> 00:20:50.158
I think she's got the idea.

00:20:51.367 --> 00:20:53.117
Rock and fire.

00:20:59.992 --> 00:21:02.450
For a beautiful girl,
that is one ugly swing.

00:21:04.742 --> 00:21:06.742
Got to follow that, huh?

00:21:17.033 --> 00:21:19.783
Don't suppose you were using
creative visualization?

00:21:20.158 --> 00:21:22.658
My face as the golf ball?

00:21:22.867 --> 00:21:24.700
Can't wait to see
your short game, buddy.

00:21:24.908 --> 00:21:28.158
- I think your ball's in the trees.
- That's bad, right?

00:21:32.783 --> 00:21:36.325
Thanks for carrying my golf bag,
Cohen. I really think I threw out my back.

00:21:36.533 --> 00:21:39.033
If your back hurts,
why don't we take a golf cart?

00:21:39.242 --> 00:21:41.158
What? Are you, like, against nature?

00:21:41.367 --> 00:21:44.242
- This isn't nature. This is a golf course.
- I have a hernia.

00:21:44.450 --> 00:21:48.408
You guys, this way we can spend
more time together as friends.

00:21:49.325 --> 00:21:52.617
How come when she says "friends,"
it sounds like a threat?

00:21:52.825 --> 00:21:54.658
It's her inflection.

00:21:56.033 --> 00:21:59.658
What? We did say we'd try and be
friends. Who's she gonna talk to? Luke?

00:21:59.867 --> 00:22:02.825
The guy only recently
learned how to walk upright.

00:22:05.867 --> 00:22:07.408
Cohen...

00:22:07.575 --> 00:22:09.242
...could you help me find my ball?

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:12.117
Anna, stay back.
There might be poison ivy.

00:22:12.283 --> 00:22:16.408
- Summer, I don't wanna get poison ivy.
- Cohen, I thought you were my friend.

00:22:17.825 --> 00:22:19.408
Okay.

00:22:22.075 --> 00:22:24.950
Looks like Summer's not
the only one who lost their balls.

00:22:30.825 --> 00:22:33.783
- Too bad.
- I could hurt that guy.

00:22:33.992 --> 00:22:36.158
So could I.

00:22:37.492 --> 00:22:41.075
Am I trying too hard with him?
All I want is to be friends.

00:22:41.283 --> 00:22:43.325
I just feel like he hates me.

00:22:44.367 --> 00:22:46.658
No. I mean... He likes you.

00:22:46.867 --> 00:22:50.075
- He just...
- Right. Trust issues.

00:22:50.283 --> 00:22:53.742
- Can't win them all, I guess.
- Hey, nobody's looking.

00:22:55.075 --> 00:22:57.617
Oh, nice shot, buddy!

00:22:57.825 --> 00:23:00.950
Okay. I think we've torn up
the course long enough.

00:23:01.158 --> 00:23:04.117
Last guy back buys the first round.

00:23:08.367 --> 00:23:10.283
Come on.

00:23:15.325 --> 00:23:17.408
Step on it. Come on.

00:23:19.908 --> 00:23:21.867
Come on, they're gaining on us.

00:23:34.950 --> 00:23:36.242
You better run!

00:23:57.742 --> 00:24:01.158
Look out! Ryan, stop, stop!

00:24:03.825 --> 00:24:06.700
Dude, nice driving.
You made that thing dance.

00:24:06.908 --> 00:24:08.533
What the hell is your problem, man?

00:24:08.742 --> 00:24:09.950
Hey, man...

00:24:10.158 --> 00:24:12.575
- I thought we were just joking.
- Yeah. Good joke.

00:24:12.783 --> 00:24:16.242
- Come down here, tell me another one.
- Oh, sorry, man.

00:24:16.450 --> 00:24:18.617
See you back at the house, okay?

00:24:21.408 --> 00:24:23.075
Are you okay?

00:24:23.283 --> 00:24:25.408
You know, he was just playing.

00:24:26.450 --> 00:24:27.658
Fine.

00:24:32.450 --> 00:24:34.742
That guy was not playing.

00:24:38.742 --> 00:24:40.742
- Hey.
- You look nice.

00:24:40.950 --> 00:24:43.367
You look like you're not
having dinner with your father.

00:24:43.575 --> 00:24:46.658
I'm gonna give them one-on-one time.
It's not a dinner I want to be at.

00:24:46.825 --> 00:24:50.408
I feel the same way about my meal.
Jimmy's right. He is done here.

00:24:50.617 --> 00:24:53.117
His best shot is starting over
somewhere else.

00:24:53.325 --> 00:24:57.908
So we'll have a nice meal, a couple
of drinks and talk about his next move.

00:24:58.117 --> 00:25:00.867
Alcohol? Yes. Inspired.

00:25:01.033 --> 00:25:03.158
How do you think
I got you to marry me?

00:25:03.367 --> 00:25:06.867
So you were drunk.
Explains everything, Kiki.

00:25:07.075 --> 00:25:08.450
Hey, Dad.

00:25:08.617 --> 00:25:11.950
It is always such a pleasure.
You two have the time of your lives.

00:25:13.742 --> 00:25:15.450
- You're not dressed.
- I'm not going.

00:25:15.617 --> 00:25:19.450
- We both know why Hailey's here.
- She wants to catch up...

00:25:19.658 --> 00:25:23.033
...with her family.
- Dad, you honestly don't believe that.

00:25:23.242 --> 00:25:26.325
Don't be jealous of your sister.
I love both my daughters equally.

00:25:26.533 --> 00:25:28.242
You don't, but that's okay.

00:25:28.408 --> 00:25:32.033
What's not okay is that she wants to take
advantage of how much you love her.

00:25:32.242 --> 00:25:35.575
- You want me to cut her off?
- I know you do too.

00:25:39.075 --> 00:25:41.742
Dinner at 6, in bed by 8.

00:25:41.950 --> 00:25:45.742
Anna, my old Jewish man
is very happy right now.

00:25:46.950 --> 00:25:49.867
It's pretty humid, Seth.
I think you could stop futzing.

00:25:50.033 --> 00:25:53.783
No. No, I can't. Futzing's what I do,
my darling. Besides, I almost have it.

00:25:55.242 --> 00:25:58.325
And there we go.
She's purring like a kitten.

00:26:00.783 --> 00:26:03.117
So, Cohen.

00:26:03.325 --> 00:26:07.367
You and me, alone in a bed.

00:26:08.325 --> 00:26:12.450
Polyfill. It's not as comfortable as down,
but it's good for our allergies, our sniffles.

00:26:13.200 --> 00:26:18.450
And this bed, huh?
It's Posturepedic for my back.

00:26:18.658 --> 00:26:20.117
And your back.

00:26:21.325 --> 00:26:23.283
- Yes?
- My catheter fell out.

00:26:24.325 --> 00:26:25.950
Hey, guys.

00:26:26.867 --> 00:26:27.908
Hey.

00:26:28.825 --> 00:26:32.283
Luke's hogging the remote,
and it's either football or porn.

00:26:32.492 --> 00:26:34.450
So could I watch TV with you guys?

00:26:34.658 --> 00:26:38.075
- We're not watching TV, Summer.
- Yeah, we were about to go to bed.

00:26:38.283 --> 00:26:40.700
- But it's 8:00. What are you, 70?
- On the inside, yes.

00:26:40.908 --> 00:26:43.908
I thought this was a weekend
where we could hang out as friends.

00:26:44.242 --> 00:26:46.033
- It is.
- Totally.

00:26:46.242 --> 00:26:48.450
Oh, I get it.

00:26:48.658 --> 00:26:51.742
It's, like, specific friend hours, right?
Whatever works for you?

00:26:51.908 --> 00:26:54.408
A friend on-off switch.
A friend appointment book.

00:26:54.617 --> 00:26:57.617
- Do I schedule friend time in advance?
- No, that is not it at all.

00:26:57.825 --> 00:26:59.908
- It's not it.
- Great. You guys.

00:27:00.242 --> 00:27:02.283
That's great.

00:27:07.325 --> 00:27:09.242
That Enrique is so hot.

00:27:09.450 --> 00:27:13.075
I mean, can you imagine
being with a guy with abs like that?

00:27:13.908 --> 00:27:16.117
Yeah, apparently not.

00:27:19.700 --> 00:27:21.783
You don't have to do that.

00:27:21.992 --> 00:27:23.908
I don't mind.

00:27:29.533 --> 00:27:31.825
Well, at least let me help.

00:27:34.075 --> 00:27:36.908
- Where's Marissa?
- Getting changed for the hot tub.

00:27:37.575 --> 00:27:39.492
You going in?

00:27:39.992 --> 00:27:41.617
Right.

00:27:42.492 --> 00:27:44.908
Can...? Can we just start over?

00:27:46.117 --> 00:27:47.408
Start over?

00:27:48.492 --> 00:27:51.158
Yeah, I feel like
we got off on the wrong foot.

00:27:51.367 --> 00:27:57.283
And I wanna make this right. Get this
thing straight, so we can be friends.

00:27:58.033 --> 00:27:59.283
What can I do?

00:27:59.950 --> 00:28:02.617
Next time you wanna be
alone with my girlfriend...

00:28:02.825 --> 00:28:05.033
...let me know so I can stay home.

00:28:09.742 --> 00:28:11.950
This always happens.

00:28:13.367 --> 00:28:17.242
Natalie. My friends at Pacific.
And now you.

00:28:17.950 --> 00:28:19.408
I'm so stupid!

00:28:19.575 --> 00:28:21.867
- Take it easy.
- Damn it!

00:28:24.825 --> 00:28:28.283
Everybody who knows me for more
than five minutes ends up hating my guts.

00:28:28.492 --> 00:28:31.158
- That's not true. Nobody hates your guts.
- What's going on?

00:28:31.325 --> 00:28:33.367
We were... We were talking.

00:28:34.658 --> 00:28:36.992
- Are you okay?
- Yeah, I'm...

00:28:37.200 --> 00:28:39.450
I'm gonna go get some
fresh air and...

00:28:39.658 --> 00:28:41.700
- I'll get some stuff for breakfast.
- I'll go too.

00:28:41.908 --> 00:28:45.950
No, just... Just stay with Ryan.
I'll be back soon. Just...

00:28:46.158 --> 00:28:49.492
Just leave the kitchen, man.
Everything's okay.

00:28:51.367 --> 00:28:53.450
You managed to drive him
out of his own house?

00:28:53.658 --> 00:28:55.950
I don't know.
We were talking, and he went off.

00:28:56.158 --> 00:28:59.783
What were you talking about
that was so upsetting?

00:28:59.992 --> 00:29:02.033
- You.
- Me?

00:29:02.575 --> 00:29:04.117
You and him.

00:29:04.325 --> 00:29:07.742
You know what? Oliver's got problems,
but you're the one who's paranoid.

00:29:08.158 --> 00:29:10.158
- What's your problem?
- I don't know.

00:29:10.367 --> 00:29:12.742
Maybe that you spent the ride
telling him about me.

00:29:12.950 --> 00:29:16.575
I wasn't. I was talking about my life.
And you're part of my life.

00:29:18.492 --> 00:29:21.700
You know what? I don't understand
what's going on with you.

00:29:24.950 --> 00:29:29.242
- There's gotta be more I can do.
- Sandy, you've done everything you can.

00:29:29.408 --> 00:29:30.533
- No, no.
- You know what?

00:29:30.742 --> 00:29:32.908
You're right, it's for the best.

00:29:33.117 --> 00:29:35.492
Like you said, I can start over,
have a new life.

00:29:35.700 --> 00:29:38.908
I never really wanted to be
a financial planner. Or a thief.

00:29:39.117 --> 00:29:42.117
Okay, so figure out right now.
What is it you really wanna do?

00:29:42.283 --> 00:29:46.408
What I really wanna do is not be
40 years old, divorced, with two kids...

00:29:46.575 --> 00:29:48.950
...and trying to figure out
what I really want to do.

00:29:49.158 --> 00:29:51.450
- What is it you used to want to be?
- A pilot.

00:29:51.658 --> 00:29:55.617
You know, I always liked
stewardesses. You?

00:29:55.825 --> 00:29:59.242
I always wanted to be left fielder
for the New York Yankees.

00:29:59.450 --> 00:30:01.783
It was that dream that
carried me through law school.

00:30:02.325 --> 00:30:06.367
The most enjoyable job I ever had,
actually, was working here.

00:30:06.575 --> 00:30:11.367
Yeah. I managed this place
the summer I married Julie.

00:30:11.575 --> 00:30:15.117
- And look at it now. It's closing.
- I mean, John Wayne used to come here.

00:30:15.325 --> 00:30:16.408
- Gary Cooper.
- Yeah.

00:30:16.617 --> 00:30:20.450
This is the real deal, you know.
This is the last bit of old Newport.

00:30:20.658 --> 00:30:24.283
Look at it, all it needs
is just a little facelift.

00:30:24.492 --> 00:30:28.283
The land value alone would be enough
to secure a decent renovation loan.

00:30:28.492 --> 00:30:33.617
You know, you update the menu a little
bit, you bring back happy hour, it'd be...

00:30:33.825 --> 00:30:36.825
- It would be fun.
- The kids would come in. It'd be fantastic.

00:30:36.992 --> 00:30:39.117
I mean, a lot more fun
than whatever...

00:30:39.325 --> 00:30:42.242
...high-priced nuisance lawsuit
I got waiting for me on my desk.

00:30:42.408 --> 00:30:45.700
A lot more fun than moving
to Phoenix without my kids.

00:30:51.158 --> 00:30:53.033
What?

00:30:53.242 --> 00:30:54.450
Katie!

00:30:55.033 --> 00:30:56.658
Two more martinis, please.

00:30:56.825 --> 00:30:58.867
Egg McMuffins.

00:30:59.075 --> 00:31:01.617
- Sounds so good.
- Why can't they serve those all day?

00:31:01.825 --> 00:31:06.117
Totally. Like, what technological
innovation is preventing that?

00:31:06.325 --> 00:31:08.200
They can put a man
on the moon, correct?

00:31:08.408 --> 00:31:11.158
And they can't serve
an Egg McMuffin past 10:30 a.m.

00:31:11.367 --> 00:31:13.075
Can't figure it out.
It doesn't make sense.

00:31:13.283 --> 00:31:15.242
Cabbage Patch Kids.

00:31:15.450 --> 00:31:20.783
They still sell those? I don't get the legend
of the cabbage patch. It freaks me out.

00:31:20.950 --> 00:31:23.200
What? Babies harvested
from the heads of cabbage?

00:31:23.408 --> 00:31:25.283
- Exactly.
- What's so freaky about that?

00:31:25.492 --> 00:31:27.283
It's all about
some child-slavery ring.

00:31:27.492 --> 00:31:29.617
It's disgusting.
It makes me want to vomit.

00:31:30.492 --> 00:31:33.325
Smurfs, dude.

00:31:33.533 --> 00:31:36.033
Do you know how tall they were?
Three apples.

00:31:36.242 --> 00:31:38.575
- Really?
- Three apples.

00:31:38.783 --> 00:31:43.158
There should be a channel on television,
I think, of us watching television.

00:31:43.325 --> 00:31:44.450
- We're that good.
- Yeah.

00:31:45.075 --> 00:31:47.450
Yeah, you are. You're so that good.

00:31:47.658 --> 00:31:51.533
Your whole witty-banter thing
is so cute, you guys.

00:31:51.742 --> 00:31:54.658
You guys are like brother and sister.

00:31:54.867 --> 00:31:57.533
Yeah, you guys could totally
be related.

00:31:57.700 --> 00:32:00.242
I'm gonna go to bed.

00:32:08.700 --> 00:32:10.867
I'm going to bed too.

00:32:23.158 --> 00:32:25.117
Hey.

00:32:25.825 --> 00:32:30.492
- He's not back yet?
- No. And he still hasn't called.

00:32:31.658 --> 00:32:33.825
I'm really worried.
It's been two hours.

00:32:34.033 --> 00:32:38.742
- What's wrong with him, exactly?
- He's been battling depression for a while.

00:32:40.242 --> 00:32:44.117
And he's had some
substance-abuse problems.

00:32:46.408 --> 00:32:47.950
I'm sorry.

00:32:48.658 --> 00:32:49.950
I just hope he's okay.

00:32:52.533 --> 00:32:54.700
It's him.

00:32:54.908 --> 00:32:57.117
- Hey.
- Marissa...

00:32:57.325 --> 00:32:59.117
...something happened.

00:32:59.283 --> 00:33:00.867
What's wrong? What is it?

00:33:01.617 --> 00:33:04.533
- I messed up real bad.
- Where are you?

00:33:04.992 --> 00:33:07.867
- What did you do?
I just drove back to Newport...

00:33:08.075 --> 00:33:10.908
...and took a whole bunch of pills.

00:33:11.075 --> 00:33:12.117
Whole bunch.

00:33:12.325 --> 00:33:15.075
- Call an ambulance.
- No, no. No doctors.

00:33:15.283 --> 00:33:19.242
- Please. Just...
- I'm so scared right now.

00:33:20.658 --> 00:33:22.450
Maybe I could throw them up.

00:33:22.617 --> 00:33:24.408
Do that.
Just get them out of your system.

00:33:24.617 --> 00:33:26.617
I'll try.

00:33:26.825 --> 00:33:28.283
But...

00:33:28.450 --> 00:33:30.158
...do you think you could...

00:33:30.367 --> 00:33:31.742
...come back?

00:33:31.950 --> 00:33:34.783
I'm sorry, but I am so scared.

00:33:35.075 --> 00:33:37.533
Okay, we're leaving right now.
See you soon.

00:33:37.742 --> 00:33:40.658
- He's not okay.
- He just took a bunch of pills.

00:33:47.742 --> 00:33:50.742
- He's not picking up.
- It's okay. You just talked to him.

00:33:50.908 --> 00:33:52.283
That was 20 minutes ago.

00:33:53.492 --> 00:33:55.658
Hi. Marissa Cooper
for Oliver Trask, please.

00:34:06.117 --> 00:34:08.867
- I thought you said he was okay.
- He said he was.

00:34:09.075 --> 00:34:10.867
He said he spent the last hour
in the bathroom...

00:34:11.075 --> 00:34:13.575
...getting the pills
out of his system.

00:34:13.783 --> 00:34:15.867
- But if that's true...
- What?

00:34:16.075 --> 00:34:18.117
Why isn't he picking up?

00:34:57.408 --> 00:35:00.742
What the hell did you say to Dad?
I know you're behind this.

00:35:01.408 --> 00:35:04.783
Hailey, we had a conversation
and we both agreed...

00:35:04.992 --> 00:35:09.617
How convenient that the one thing you
two agree on is how to screw me over.

00:35:10.033 --> 00:35:13.783
- Hailey, you don't have to do this.
- I thought this is what you wanted.

00:35:13.992 --> 00:35:17.492
Me not taking Dad's money
or taking up room in your house.

00:35:17.700 --> 00:35:19.867
I never said that you couldn't stay.

00:35:20.075 --> 00:35:23.825
No. You said you wanted me to live my
own life, be on my own, be independent.

00:35:24.033 --> 00:35:26.700
Then you went and sabotaged
my relationship with Dad.

00:35:26.867 --> 00:35:30.700
What relationship with Dad? You take
his money and then you take off.

00:35:30.908 --> 00:35:34.783
My relationship with Dad
is between me and Dad.

00:35:34.992 --> 00:35:38.200
- Was between me and Dad.
- I just don't wanna see you in trouble.

00:35:38.408 --> 00:35:40.742
Well, now you won't have to.

00:35:44.033 --> 00:35:45.992
There's my cab.

00:35:46.367 --> 00:35:50.742
Oh, Hailey, where are you gonna go?
You don't have any money.

00:35:50.950 --> 00:35:54.992
Yeah, well, whose fault is that?
I'll find another way to get by.

00:35:55.200 --> 00:35:58.033
- You could stay here and work for Dad.
- Why?

00:35:58.200 --> 00:35:59.992
So I can be as independent as you are?

00:36:00.158 --> 00:36:03.867
Living off his money
in the McMansion he built you?

00:36:05.033 --> 00:36:06.742
I'm sorry...

00:36:06.950 --> 00:36:10.033
...but you were right.
I need to have my own life.

00:36:10.242 --> 00:36:13.575
And the only way that I can do that
is to get as far away from Dad...

00:36:13.783 --> 00:36:16.200
...and as far away from you as I can.

00:36:18.575 --> 00:36:19.950
I'll see you.

00:36:29.200 --> 00:36:32.200
Oliver. Open up, please.

00:36:32.367 --> 00:36:34.242
It's me.

00:36:35.533 --> 00:36:38.700
- We have to call security.
- I'll go.

00:36:38.908 --> 00:36:41.742
Oliver. Oh, my God. You're okay.

00:36:41.950 --> 00:36:43.950
Yeah, kind of.

00:36:44.367 --> 00:36:46.867
- You all right, man?
- Yeah. A little embarrassed.

00:36:47.075 --> 00:36:51.575
- When you didn't pick up the phone, l...
- I was in the shower. Sorry about that.

00:36:51.783 --> 00:36:55.325
I got kind of messed up,
but I'm good now.

00:36:55.533 --> 00:36:56.908
Yeah.

00:36:57.075 --> 00:36:59.200
You guys should go,
enjoy the rest of the weekend.

00:36:59.408 --> 00:37:03.992
What are you talking about?
We're not going anywhere.

00:37:06.033 --> 00:37:08.867
So, what did you take exactly?

00:37:09.075 --> 00:37:11.908
I don't know.

00:37:12.117 --> 00:37:16.075
A bunch of sleeping pills,
some painkillers.

00:37:16.658 --> 00:37:18.700
Well, how many?

00:37:18.908 --> 00:37:23.408
I don't remember. But I got them
all out of my system, I promise.

00:37:23.617 --> 00:37:27.408
Well, did you drink any water?
Because you're probably dehydrated.

00:37:27.617 --> 00:37:31.075
You know, we should call room service.
You want any ginger ale or Gatorade?

00:37:31.283 --> 00:37:33.825
Maybe we should take him
to the emergency room. I mean...

00:37:34.033 --> 00:37:36.117
...he swallowed all those pills.

00:37:36.325 --> 00:37:38.700
If they were in my system,
I'd have felt them by now.

00:37:38.908 --> 00:37:43.408
Yeah, but why take any chances?
We can take you now.

00:37:43.617 --> 00:37:47.658
The thing is, if we go
to the emergency room...

00:37:47.867 --> 00:37:50.783
...they'll put me under suicide watch
for 72 hours.

00:37:50.950 --> 00:37:54.367
They'll call the cops, and then
they'll call my parents in Zurich.

00:37:54.575 --> 00:37:56.950
I mean, the truth is that I'm fine.

00:37:57.158 --> 00:38:01.867
Really. I just want to just crawl into my
bed and forget this day ever happened.

00:38:23.158 --> 00:38:26.242
- Sandy.
- Hey, you're awake.

00:38:26.450 --> 00:38:28.158
Oh, shoot!

00:38:28.367 --> 00:38:31.575
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

00:38:31.783 --> 00:38:32.908
Are you drunk?

00:38:34.117 --> 00:38:37.658
- Don't worry, I took a cab.
- Yeah, so did Hailey.

00:38:37.867 --> 00:38:40.533
Dad cut her off, and she cut me off.

00:38:40.700 --> 00:38:42.325
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:38:42.492 --> 00:38:44.367
So how was your night?

00:38:44.575 --> 00:38:46.367
That good, huh?

00:38:46.533 --> 00:38:48.783
You know, I'm not sure, but...

00:38:50.200 --> 00:38:53.200
I think Jimmy and I might have
gone into business together tonight.

00:38:53.575 --> 00:38:56.325
Really?
And what kind of business is that?

00:38:56.492 --> 00:38:57.575
The restaurant business.

00:38:57.783 --> 00:39:01.617
- Oh, you are drunk.
- In an adorable way, I think. Yeah?

00:39:03.408 --> 00:39:07.158
- And what about the firm?
- They'll have my body.

00:39:07.367 --> 00:39:10.492
And so will you, by the way.

00:39:10.700 --> 00:39:15.200
But the restaurant will have
my soul and my income.

00:39:15.408 --> 00:39:18.533
- And my savings.
- How can you do that?

00:39:18.742 --> 00:39:20.992
Look, I'm making more money
than I ever made in my life...

00:39:21.200 --> 00:39:22.825
...and I'm having way less fun.

00:39:23.033 --> 00:39:25.700
I used to help people for a living,
you remember that.

00:39:27.658 --> 00:39:32.367
I'll tell you, your buddy Jimmy Cooper,
man, he needs some help.

00:39:32.575 --> 00:39:36.367
Oh, man, if he doesn't get a job,
he's gonna have to leave town.

00:39:36.575 --> 00:39:38.450
I don't want him to leave town.

00:39:38.658 --> 00:39:42.617
You know, it's been a long time
since I've had a friend in Newport.

00:39:42.825 --> 00:39:46.617
I don't want to have to find
another friend in Newport. Am I crazy?

00:39:49.367 --> 00:39:51.825
Oh, I'm crazy.

00:39:52.033 --> 00:39:55.242
You have to be crazy
to be in the restaurant business.

00:39:56.492 --> 00:39:58.700
But I think it's great
that you wanna help Jimmy.

00:39:58.908 --> 00:40:00.033
Well, you know...

00:40:00.242 --> 00:40:04.867
And be friends after all this time,
it means a lot to me.

00:40:11.992 --> 00:40:13.700
Sandy?

00:40:22.700 --> 00:40:25.075
They're sleeping.

00:40:29.908 --> 00:40:32.492
Hey, we're home.

00:40:34.867 --> 00:40:37.283
Thanks for the ride, buddy.
Great weekend, huh?

00:40:37.492 --> 00:40:39.033
- Bye, Summer.
- Bye.

00:40:39.200 --> 00:40:41.950
See you guys. Have fun. Drive safely.

00:40:45.700 --> 00:40:47.492
So you're into Cohen, huh?

00:40:47.658 --> 00:40:49.658
It must be kind of weird
to see him with somebody else.

00:40:49.867 --> 00:40:53.242
- It was for me with Marissa.
- Whatevs.

00:40:53.450 --> 00:40:57.200
I'm over it. Moving on.
Ready for my next victim.

00:40:57.783 --> 00:40:59.575
Well, just for the record...

00:40:59.783 --> 00:41:02.700
...whoever he turns out to be,
he's a lucky dude.

00:41:02.867 --> 00:41:05.533
You're looking pretty hot
these days, Summer.

00:41:06.742 --> 00:41:08.450
Real hot.

00:41:08.992 --> 00:41:10.700
Thanks.

00:41:13.908 --> 00:41:15.992
Oh, my God!

00:41:16.200 --> 00:41:20.325
Oh, God, I'm sorry, Luke. You're cute
and everything, but there's just no way.

00:41:23.700 --> 00:41:25.325
No worries.

00:41:37.950 --> 00:41:40.617
What are you doing?
What are you looking for?

00:41:40.825 --> 00:41:42.533
Nothing. Is he gonna be all right?

00:41:42.700 --> 00:41:45.158
Yeah. I think so.
I told him I'd stay tonight.

00:41:45.908 --> 00:41:47.867
- What?
- Well, I can't leave him alone.

00:41:48.075 --> 00:41:50.033
What if he tries it again?

00:41:50.242 --> 00:41:53.533
- Lf he tried it the first time.
- What?

00:41:54.117 --> 00:41:56.617
What if he didn't try
to kill himself tonight?

00:41:56.825 --> 00:41:58.783
- What?
- He wouldn't go to the hospital.

00:41:58.992 --> 00:42:01.825
Maybe he didn't want to be
shipped off to an institution.

00:42:01.992 --> 00:42:05.408
Maybe he belongs there.
I mean, what kind of person does this?

00:42:06.617 --> 00:42:09.450
- No, not... I didn't mean...
- You should go.

00:42:09.658 --> 00:42:12.658
- You weren't trying to kill yourself.
- Maybe Oliver wasn't either.

00:42:12.867 --> 00:42:16.825
But he's my friend,
and I can't leave him alone tonight.

00:42:17.033 --> 00:42:21.533
So, you know what, just go home,
and I'll see you in the morning.

00:42:22.033 --> 00:42:23.950
Sorry to interrupt.

00:42:24.908 --> 00:42:27.575
I just want to say thanks, Ryan.
For everything, man.

00:42:27.992 --> 00:42:30.492
Sorry for ruining your weekend.

00:42:32.033 --> 00:42:33.867
Good night.

00:42:38.950 --> 00:42:41.158
I'll call you tomorrow.
